@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<section class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
        <nav class="breadcrumb-nav">
            <a asp-action="Index">Home</a>
            <span>/</span>
            <span>Privacy Policy</span>
        </nav>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p>Your privacy matters to us. Learn how we collect, use, and protect your personal information.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="content-section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="content-card fade-in">
            <p><em>Last updated: June 12, 2026</em></p>

            <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
            <p>
                Aloha Resort ("we", "our", or "us"), operating at aloha-resort.com, is committed to protecting your privacy.
                This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your information when
                you visit our website or use our services at any of our casino hotel properties.
            </p>

            <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
            <p>We may collect the following types of personal information:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Contact Information:</strong> Name, email address, phone number, and mailing address.</li>
                <li><strong>Reservation Data:</strong> Booking details, check-in/check-out dates, room preferences, and payment information.</li>
                <li><strong>Account Information:</strong> Username, password, and loyalty program membership details.</li>
                <li><strong>Technical Data:</strong> IP address, browser type, device information, and cookies.</li>
                <li><strong>Gaming Data:</strong> Casino membership information as required by Hawaii gaming regulations.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
            <p>We use the collected information for the following purposes:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Processing reservations and providing hotel and casino services</li>
                <li>Communicating with you about your bookings and inquiries</li>
                <li>Improving our website, services, and customer experience</li>
                <li>Complying with legal obligations under U.S. federal and Hawaii state law</li>
                <li>Sending promotional materials (with your consent)</li>
                <li>Preventing fraud and ensuring responsible gaming compliance</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>4. Legal Basis for Processing</h2>
            <p>
                Under the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), we process your personal data based on:
                contractual necessity, legal obligations, legitimate interests, and your explicit consent where applicable.
            </p>

            <h2>5. Data Sharing</h2>
            <p>
                We do not sell your personal information. We may share data with trusted third-party service providers
                (payment processors, booking platforms) and regulatory authorities as required by U.S. gaming and
                hospitality laws. All third parties are bound by data protection agreements.
            </p>

            <h2>6. Data Retention</h2>
            <p>
                We retain personal data only as long as necessary to fulfill the purposes outlined in this policy,
                comply with legal obligations, and resolve disputes. Gaming-related records are retained as required
                by applicable U.S. gaming authority regulations.
            </p>

            <h2>7. Your Rights</h2>
            <p>Under GDPR, you have the right to:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Access your personal data</li>
                <li>Rectify inaccurate information</li>
                <li>Request deletion of your data ("right to be forgotten")</li>
                <li>Restrict or object to processing</li>
                <li>Data portability</li>
                <li>Withdraw consent at any time</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>8. Cookies</h2>
            <p>
                Our website uses cookies to enhance your browsing experience. You can manage cookie preferences
                through your browser settings. Essential cookies are required for the website to function properly.
            </p>

            <h2>9. Security</h2>
            <p>
                We implement industry-standard security measures including encryption, secure servers, and access
                controls to protect your personal information from unauthorized access, alteration, or disclosure.
            </p>

            <h2>10. Contact Us</h2>
            <p>
                If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or wish to exercise your data rights, please contact
                our Data Protection Officer at <strong>privacy@aloha-resort.com</strong> or write to us at
                2255 Kalakaua Ave, Honolulu, HI 96815.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
